        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e12ff12d-9cb6-3171-b2f5-1e17f3625793",
                "word": "anderzijds",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ba95753-ddd6-3efe-9bec-905698912dc7",
                        "entry_id": "e12ff12d-9cb6-3171-b2f5-1e17f3625793",
                        "glosses": [
                            "aan de andere kant"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "maar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "159efd37-dfc1-43c0-9622-daa73674094a",
                                "sense_id": "1ba95753-ddd6-3efe-9bec-905698912dc7",
                                "text": "Enerzijds was hij teleurgesteld over de matige opkomst en anderzijds was hij tevreden over de geweldige sfeer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad45f3b8-e60c-459e-add7-fe989bc31524",
                                "sense_id": "1ba95753-ddd6-3efe-9bec-905698912dc7",
                                "text": "In veel winkels zijn ondertussen lege schappen te vinden. Vooral versproducten als zuivel, vlees, fruit en eieren zijn nog moeilijk te krijgen. Dat komt enerzijds doordat de blokkades het onmogelijk maken om de producten aan te vullen en anderzijds doordat de producten die nog beschikbaar zijn bederven en dus weggegooid moeten worden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "106ae0a6-b33d-42d5-8ef0-f7ec1176150b",
                                "sense_id": "1ba95753-ddd6-3efe-9bec-905698912dc7",
                                "text": "Enerzijds is de invloed van grote culturen op elke hoek van de straat zichtbaar, anderzijds heeft Palermo het laagste inkomen per hoofd en de hoogste werkloosheid van Italië."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aaac5e08-7ad3-44ec-857a-b7fc36b9d293",
                        "source_entry_id": "e12ff12d-9cb6-3171-b2f5-1e17f3625793",
                        "source_sense_id": "1ba95753-ddd6-3efe-9bec-905698912dc7",
                        "source_sense_description": "(maar) aan de andere kant",
                        "target_lang_word": "andererseits",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "andererseits",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e3280b8-3e4f-3f44-9f62-d35c4178aa18",
                                        "entry_id": "ab85da86-368e-3d5a-81b6-dc322003c444",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Adverb, das ein Thema in eine Zweigeteiltheit kategorisiert, von der die zweite Seite folgt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c52b51e-3ae3-4f16-8de5-4f8823a7c838",
                                                "sense_id": "3e3280b8-3e4f-3f44-9f62-d35c4178aa18",
                                                "text": "Einerseits gefällt mir dein Vorhaben, andererseits bezweifle ich jedoch die Umsetzbarkeit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "384dbdcc-6e0b-4f80-95a2-29c04fa279d2",
                                                "sense_id": "3e3280b8-3e4f-3f44-9f62-d35c4178aa18",
                                                "text": "„Andererseits war Bertillon hochintelligent.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db822f6c-0b7a-4c77-9110-2b40e8b74cf4",
                                                "sense_id": "3e3280b8-3e4f-3f44-9f62-d35c4178aa18",
                                                "text": "„Einerseits war die Stadt tatsächlich nicht mehr durch die gewöhnlichen Verkehrsmittel mit dem übrigen Land verbunden, und andererseits untersagte eine neue Verordnung jeglichen Briefwechsel, um zu verhüten, daß die Briefe zu Infektionsträgern würden.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b4470e87-ebdc-4cd4-b0e2-781c7c63c951",
                        "source_entry_id": "e12ff12d-9cb6-3171-b2f5-1e17f3625793",
                        "source_sense_id": "1ba95753-ddd6-3efe-9bec-905698912dc7",
                        "source_sense_description": "(maar) aan de andere kant",
                        "target_lang_word": "on the other hand",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "on the other hand",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2a93214-1d6f-315b-a104-6d6c92249abe",
                                        "entry_id": "4023947a-098c-3d8c-9ab9-9275c83233c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "From another point of view."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "sequence"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6002650-02f7-4f82-97d5-51dcaa029ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "d2a93214-1d6f-315b-a104-6d6c92249abe",
                                                "text": "Well yes, it was quite a good bargain; on the other hand, do we really need one?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37c7fca4-7e78-47f9-aeb2-b1c778d818c1",
                                                "sense_id": "d2a93214-1d6f-315b-a104-6d6c92249abe",
                                                "text": "Its external relations, on the one hand to dynamics, and on the other to heat, light, chemical action, and the constitution of bodies, seem to indicate the special importance of electrical science as an aid to the interpretation of nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "821c1668-c657-465f-b5ac-c8405d8a33bf",
                                                "sense_id": "d2a93214-1d6f-315b-a104-6d6c92249abe",
                                                "text": "Thus the study of the language he is supposed to use, to the average American, takes on a sort of bilingual character. On the one hand, he is grounded abominably in a grammar and syntax that have always been largely artificial, even in the country where they are supposed to prevail, and on the other hand he has to pick up the essentials of his actual speech as best he may."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbb446f6-34b8-438f-b371-13f076967df6",
                                                "sense_id": "d2a93214-1d6f-315b-a104-6d6c92249abe",
                                                "text": "1950, Bertrand Russell, acceptance speech for Nobel Prize in Literature\nI maintain, however, on the one hand, that there are few occasions upon which large bodies of men, such as politics is concerned with, can rise above selfishness, while, on the other hand, there are a very great many circumstances in which populations will fall below selfishness, if selfishness is interpreted as enlightened self-interest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c54a69e4-937e-4b7f-9f9b-5667c6e45773",
                                                "sense_id": "d2a93214-1d6f-315b-a104-6d6c92249abe",
                                                "text": "The host of business travellers between Bishops Stortford and London would scarcely take kindly to devious routing via the Southbury line; on the other hand, it is not desirable that they should overcrowd the business trains to and from Cambridge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
